---
title: Web Deployment Modes - OmniSign (same-origin and split-origin)
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 30
    rankSpacing: 45
    wrappingWidth: 460
---
flowchart TB
  subgraph A["a) Shared reverse proxy - the web app and the API share one origin"]
    direction TB
    BRA["Browser"]
    RPA["Reverse proxy<br/>TLS termination"]
    WEBA["Web bundle (static files)<br/>Wasm + JS + web-config.json"]
    SRVA["OmniSign Server<br/>Ktor / Netty"]
    BRA -->|"HTTPS"| RPA
    RPA -->|"everything else (static)"| WEBA
    RPA -->|"/api/v1"| SRVA
  end

  subgraph B["b) Separate origins - the browser talks to two hosts, so CORS applies"]
    direction TB
    BRB["Browser"]
    WEBB["Web bundle (static files)<br/>on its own origin"]
    SRVB["OmniSign Server<br/>own TLS or its own proxy,<br/>a second host or a second port"]
    BRB -->|"HTTPS"| WEBB
    BRB -->|"HTTPS + CORS preflight"| SRVB
  end

  NOTEA["web-config.json absent, or its url empty, means same origin.<br/>The refresh cookie is then first-party, so allowCredentials can stay false."]
  NOTEB["web-config.json supplies url (and the optional organizationName branding),<br/>which retargets a pre-built bundle without recompiling it.<br/>cors.allowedOrigins must list the web origin, and allowCredentials: true is what<br/>lets /auth/refresh receive the cookie - without it login still works, but every<br/>page load falls back to a full round trip through the identity provider."]
  GUARD["Both modes must configure cors.allowedOrigins deliberately:<br/>a missing cors: block and an empty list are each rejected at startup,<br/>and allowCredentials: true combined with the * wildcard is refused,<br/>because Ktor reflects the caller's Origin instead of emitting a literal *"]

  SRVA -.-> NOTEA
  SRVB -.-> NOTEB

